      "content": "Yes, option B is correct! 🎉\n\n**Final Answer:** B\n\n---\n### 📖 Formula Breakdown (How It Works):\n* **The Formula:** $F_{\\text{net}} = ma$\n* **What the letters mean:**\n  * $F_{\\text{net}}$: The total force acting on the object (in Newtons, N)\n  * $m$: The mass of the object (in kilograms, kg)\n  * $a$: The acceleration of the object (in meters per second squared, m·s⁻²)\n* **Why we use it:** This formula shows that the net force and acceleration are directly proportional and always point in the same direction. The direction of motion is irrelevant—what matters is the direction of acceleration.\n\n🎯 **Exam Tip:** In DBE exams, always double-check the direction of acceleration when answering questions about net force. Mixing up motion and acceleration directions is a common mistake!"
